    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter May 31 with a high-ceiling lineup centered on prime matchups against Imai and Kochanowicz. **Christian Yelich** (75.84) and **Junior Caminero** (73.35) headline the slate, both benefiting from elite SP skill indicators (5.17 xERA) and advantageous dynamic platoon splits. While the scarcity of stolen bases remains our primary concern, the presence of **Casey Schmitt** (63.92) is pivotal today; he draws a favorable matchup against Gordon and earns a +2% efficiency bump specifically due to the opposing pitcher\u2019s slow delivery, which maximizes his SB upside. **Colt Keith** (63.27) rounds out our top-tier targets, as his lead-off spot against Burke provides the highest projected floor in the infield.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Chase Meidroth** (50.42), who was excluded despite a favorable matchup against Montero. Ultimately, **Chase Meidroth** fell just short of the efficiency threshold when compared to the high-leverage spots occupied by **Gary Sanchez** and **Caleb Durbin**, whose respective SP matchups and lineup security offered more predictable production. We are navigating significant headwinds at the top of the order, specifically with **Trea Turner** (53.46) and **Kyle Schwarber** (54.85) facing a formidable arm in Yamamoto. While wind assistance provides a slight buffer for both, the elite skill level of the opposing starter introduces a non-trivial risk of an early exit or suppressed counting stats. We will continue to monitor the status of **Lars Nootbaar** and **Hyeseong Kim**, but for now, the active roster remains optimized to exploit the specific xERA vulnerabilities presented in today\u2019s rotation.",
